Google Dorking Intelligence Guide

Google Dorking:----  i)  intext: — finds the word inside page body text
                     ii) intitle: — finds the word inside the page title
                     iii) inurl: — finds the word inside the URL
                     iv) site: — restricts results to a specific website only
                      v)  -site: — excludes a specific website from results
                     vi) cache: — shows Google's last saved version of a page
                     vii) filetype: — searches for a specific file type like pdf, doc, csv
                     viii) OR — finds pages matching either of two terms
                     ix) AND — finds pages matching both terms together
                     x)  " " (quotes) — searches for exact phrase only, no variations
                     xi) (asterisk) — wildcard, fills in any word in that position
                     xii) (minus) — excludes a word from results
                     xiii) related: — finds websites similar to a given site
                     xiv) link: — finds pages that link to a specific URL
                     xv) before: — filters results published before a specific date
                     xvi) after: — filters results published after a specific date
                     
                     
